@rupic-app Fixed in 94a473b6e (committed locally, in the next push). Labels compared against `Date.now()` per render while the primitive memoized its window per `data`; HeatGraph now takes one `end` per `data`, passes it to `Root` as the window end, and labels against it. Repro test: re-render after midnight added a label over the last column.

This makes labels and cells agree across re-renders. It does not remove the SSR case: the window end still comes from the clock when the component first renders, on the server and again on the client, exactly as the cells did on `main`. Making that hydration-stable needs an `end` input from the app (or a stable default in the `heat-graph` package), which is an API change I'd keep separate.

