comment.body:
Valid. Fixed locally in fbd768e0a (not pushed yet); the change for this line:

```suggestion
        void response.body?.cancel().catch(() => undefined);
```

The abort-while-the-handler-runs path (line 163) had the same `await`, which kept the request id in `inflight` indefinitely, so it gets the same change:

```diff
-        await response.body?.cancel().catch(() => undefined);
+        void response.body?.cancel().catch(() => undefined);
```

New tests, both failing before the change: "ends a HEAD response whose body never finishes cancelling" and "frees the id of an aborted request whose response never finishes cancelling".

