@rupic-app Agreed the finding was valid. The fix is on this PR's branch, not on `main`: https://github.com/assistant-ui/assistant-ui/pull/8689/commits/500ed1d33

The relevant change in `image-gallery.tsx`:

```diff
   const focusDialog = useCallback((node: HTMLDivElement | null) => {
-    node?.focus();
+    node?.closest<HTMLElement>('[role="dialog"]')?.focus();
   }, []);
```

```diff
-          <DialogContent
-            ref={focusDialog}
-            className="gap-3 p-3 duration-150 motion-reduce:animate-none sm:max-w-[min(56rem,calc(100%-2rem))]"
-          >
+          <DialogContent className="gap-3 p-3 duration-150 motion-reduce:animate-none sm:max-w-[min(56rem,calc(100%-2rem))]">
             <DialogTitle className="sr-only">
               Image {index + 1} of {images.length}
             </DialogTitle>
-            <div className="flex min-h-0 items-center justify-center px-10">
+            <div
+              ref={focusDialog}
+              className="flex min-h-0 items-center justify-center px-10"
+            >
```

The ref now sits on a host `div` the gallery owns, so it arrives on React 18 with either dialog wrapper. `image-gallery.test.tsx` mocks a `DialogContent` that drops `ref`; the focus-on-open test failed with that mock before this change.

